# 1️⃣ Cycle in a Graph

A cycle exists if we can return to the same node after traversing edges.

Example:

```text
1 ---- 2
|      |
|      |
4 ---- 3
```

Cycle:

```text
1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 1
```

---

# 2️⃣ Cycle Detection in Undirected Graph using BFS

## Idea

Store:

```text
Node
Parent
```

If we visit a node that is already visited and is NOT the parent, then a cycle exists.

---

### Example

```text
1 ---- 2
|      |
4 ---- 3
```

Start BFS from:

```text
1
```

Eventually:

```text
3 sees 4

4 already visited

4 is not parent

Cycle Found
```

---

## C++ Code

```cpp
bool detectCycleBFS(
    int start,
    vector<int> adj[],
    vector<int>& vis)
{
    queue<pair<int,int>> q;

    vis[start] = 1;

    q.push({start, -1});

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        auto current = q.front();

        q.pop();

        int node = current.first;
        int parent = current.second;

        for(int neighbor : adj[node])
        {
            if(!vis[neighbor])
            {
                vis[neighbor] = 1;

                q.push({
                    neighbor,
                    node
                });
            }
            else if(neighbor != parent)
            {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }

    return false;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Cycle Detection in Undirected Graph using DFS

## Idea

While traversing:

```text
If neighbor is visited
and neighbor != parent

Cycle Exists
```

---

## C++ Code

```cpp
bool detectCycleDFS(
    int node,
    int parent,
    vector<int> adj[],
    vector<int>& vis)
{
    vis[node] = 1;

    for(int neighbor : adj[node])
    {
        if(!vis[neighbor])
        {
            if(
                detectCycleDFS(
                    neighbor,
                    node,
                    adj,
                    vis
                )
            )
            {
                return true;
            }
        }
        else if(neighbor != parent)
        {
            return true;
        }
    }

    return false;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

